    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite (only `AcceptanceTest` exists as a runnable test class) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `ownerSegment` with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **New class `OwnerSegment`** (`model/OwnerSegment.java`) \u2014 a small, cohesive unit with a single static `of(int membershipLevel, String locality)` method. TIER is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD) else `REGIONAL`. Its surrounding-class complexity (WMC_other) is zero.\n\n2. **One line added** to `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` \u2014 a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` that composes the existing `MembershipLevel` and `CustomerCode.regionOf` derivations (consistent with the existing `membershipLevel` and `locality` mappings). No existing method body was grown.\n\n3. **openapi.yml** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` schema field so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nI kept the logic out of any large class (both `Owner` and the mapper's expressions stay untouched in complexity), so the biggest cost lever (WMC_other on a large class) is avoided entirely.",
